            <div type="edition">
                <p><lb n="1"/>pesna:<name type="gentilicium">tutna</name>:velsial</p></div>
            
            <div type="translation"></div>

            <div type="commentary">
            <p>Mario Del Chiaro (who ascribed this relief to the end of the 3rd century BCE)
                    included the relief  in the book published on occasion of a 1967 exhibition of
                    Etruscan art at the Art Gallery of the University of California at Santa Barbara
                    (see bibliography), although it was not available for the exhibition. Such
                    absence explains his description of the inscription as painted in black, while
                    the photograph shows a reddish-brown color.</p>
                <p>Del Chiaro: "Terracotta cinerary urns (…) were standard mass-produced items
                    during the late 3rd and the 2nd Centuries B.C. Although the lids with reclining
                    figures were interchangeable, depending on the size of the urn, the central
                    panels decorated with reliefs were often monotonous when their themes were
                    derived from one basic original."</p></div>
            

